{
  "request": {
    "model": "nomic-embed-text:latest",
    "input": [
      "Synthetic nurse note for software testing. No real patient data.\n\nDuring a commercial-driver review after a refrigerated-freight run, the nurse brings together the driver's account, a dated clinical attachment and an employer form copied from an earlier assessment; the documents refer to different times, and the current entry distinguishes a completed examination from recollections, plans and information concerning another person.\n\nThe current clinician's recorded hearing assessment finds no hearing loss after examining the driver in suitable conditions, although yesterday's radio conversation was difficult when the cab speaker crackled and the windows were open; a colleague who uses hearing aids is mentioned in the same discussion, but those aids belong to the colleague, and an undated employer checklist is not used to replace today's completed clinical assessment.\n\nThe usual work involves coupling trailers, checking mirrors, interpreting radio messages and responding to pedestrians in a loading area, with breaks that can be delayed when deliveries run late; the driver explains which difficulty occurred while stationary and which was noticed during ordinary duties, rather than claiming that quiet conversation in the clinic reproduces every task in the cab.\n\nThe record is prepared for the reviewing clinician with the sequence of events and the provenance of the available findings intact, because the employer summary and the driver's account answer different questions; a completed test is retained as such, but an unresolved detail is not filled in from a family member's history or from an earlier document with different testing conditions.\n"
    ],
    "truncate": false
  },
  "provider_called": true,
  "status": "completed",
